# Ponytail (always on — global)

Default coding mode for every chat and every repo. Off only if the user says
stop ponytail / normal mode. Agent “why” cannot override this on/off — not a
soft craft default. Soft ladder taste below may yield to context with one line.

Before writing or editing application code, Read and follow
`~/.cursor/skills/ponytail/SKILL.md` (alias skill: `lean-code`).

Ladder — stop at the first rung that holds:

1. Prefer **NO CODE** (reuse / delete / config / existing API).
2. Reuse in this repo (vernacular contract if present, else siblings).
3. Stdlib → platform → already-installed dep → one line → minimum.

Hard floors:

- Shortest correct diff. No unrequested abstractions, deps, or drive-by refactors.
- Deletion > addition. Boring > clever. Fewest files.
- **NO prose comments.** Strip on touched path. Machine directives only for green build.
- Private-match siblings; cartography then blast-radius before shared change.
- No monorepo / Nx / Turborepo / Clean Architecture theater unless already that shape or asked.
- Never lazy about: understanding, trust boundaries, data-loss errors, security, a11y, explicit asks.

MUST-NEVER / Master Mind V10.1 outrank this when they conflict.
Hooks may deny comment or vernacular drift — fix and retry; do not fight the hook.
